-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt — the browser experiment
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer,
+compiled to real WebAssembly with Emscripten. All live rendering happens locally
+in a module Web Worker; pixels are progressively copied to a canvas. No rendering
+service or GPU API is required.
 
+## Run
 
 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm install
+pnpm dev --host 0.0.0.0
 ```
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+Open `/`. The scene renders automatically. **Randomize colors** changes both the
+walls and the mirror/glass sphere colors and starts a new render. Quality and
+resolution controls rerender the scene; the render button can stop or restart it.
+The download icon saves the displayed image as PNG.
 
-## Tech Stack
+## Build
 
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+```sh
+pnpm build
+```
+
+The homepage is prerendered to `dist/client/index.html`. The compiled Wasm,
+JavaScript loader, worker, preview, and license are included in `public/` and are
+copied into the build. `pnpm start` serves the complete Astro build.
+
+## Rebuild the C++ module
+
+Install Emscripten (`em++` on PATH), then run:
+
+```sh
+pnpm build:wasm
+pnpm check:wasm
+```
+
+`native/smallpt-original.cpp` is the unmodified upstream source. The browser
+adapter retains its integrator, sphere geometry, materials, camera, and tent
+sampling, and adds color controls and a progressive RGBA framebuffer. The original
+command-line entry point is unused. The build suppresses warnings in that legacy
+entry point, enables runtime assertions and stack checks, and reserves 2 MiB for
+the recursive integrator. Each progressive pass adds four samples per pixel.
+
+`pnpm check:wasm` executes the actual shipped binary under Node to validate pixel
+output and sphere color changes. `node scripts/check-wasm.mjs --preview` also
+regenerates the 256-spp static preview using that binary. The preview is an actual
+path traced image, not an AI-generated illustration.
+
+Original smallpt copyright © 2006–2008 Kevin Beason, MIT license. The upstream
+license is preserved in `native/LICENSE.txt` and distributed in
+`public/wasm/LICENSE.txt`.
